            "italic": false,
            "superscript": false
          }
        }
      ],
      "kind": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "content": "Nethys Note: This innovation is a part of the ",
          "kind": "text",
          "marks": {
            "bold": false,
            "italic": true,
            "superscript": false
          }
        },
        {
          "display": "Munitions Master",
          "kind": "brokenRef",
          "target": "archetype/munitions-master"
        },
        {
          "content": " archetype.",
          "kind": "text",
          "marks": {
            "bold": false,
            "italic": true,
            "superscript": false
          }
        }
      ],
      "kind": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "content": "Your innovation is a mounted siege weapon called a ",
          "kind": "text",
          "marks": {
            "bold": false,
            "italic": false,
            "superscript": false
          }
        },
        {
          "display": "light mortar",
          "kind": "crossref",
          "targetId": "siege-weapon/light-mortar"
        },
        {
          "content": " that weighs 2 Bulk. Whether it propels its payload via an elaborate mechanism or explosive reagents, it's capable of dealing immense damage. Your light mortar requires an ",
          "kind": "text",
          "marks": {
            "bold": false,
            "italic": false,
            "superscript": false
          }
        },
        {
          "display": "Interact",
          "kind": "crossref",
          "targetId": "action/interact"
        },
        {
          "content": " action to deploy it before you can Aim, Load, or Launch it, and it includes its own wheeled platform that it is mounted on as part of the deployment. It can be packed back up for easy transport as a 2-action activity with the manipulate trait and either worn as a backpack or carried in one hand while packed. Because of the light mortar's smaller size, the Move Siege Engine activity takes only 1 action when it is deployed.",
          "kind": "text",
          "marks": {
            "bold": false,
            "italic": false,
            "superscript": false
          }
        }
      ],
      "kind": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "content": "Your light mortar begins as a 1st-level siege weapon with the statistics shown below. It deals an additional die of damage at 5th level and every 4 levels thereafter. When you Launch your light mortar, the Reflex save is equal to your class DC. Its AC is equal to your inventor class DC and it has Hardness 5. It has trained proficiency in Reflex and Fortitude saves, using your Intelligence modifier to calculate these bonuses. It has 10 Hit Points, plus a number of Hit Points equal to 2 plus your Intelligence modifier for each level you have. Its Broken Threshold is equal to half its total Hit Points (rounded down).",
          "kind": "text",
          "marks": {
            "bold": false,
            "italic": false,
            "superscript": false
          }
        }
      ],
      "kind": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "content": "At 5th level, your light mortar's Hardness increases to 10. At 10th level it increases to 15 and its proficiency rank in Reflex and Fortitude saves increases to expert. At 15th level, its Hardness increases to 20, and its proficiency rank in Reflex and Fortitude saves increases to master. ",
          "kind": "text",
          "marks": {
            "bold": false,
            "italic": false,
            "superscript": false
          }
        }
      ],
      "kind": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "content": "Your ",
          "kind": "text",
          "marks": {
            "bold": false,
            "italic": false,
            "superscript": false
          }
        },
        {
          "display": "innovation",
          "kind": "crossref",
          "targetId": "siege-weapon/light-mortar"
        },
        {
          "content": " fires small cannonballs called carry shot. A group of 10 carry shot, which weighs 1 Bulk, can be purchased for 5 sp from most shops that sell ammunition. ",
          "kind": "text",
          "marks": {
            "bold": false,
            "italic": false,
            "superscript": false
          }
        }
      ],
      "kind": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "content": "Choose one initial light mortar modification to apply to your innovation, either from the following or from other initial light mortar modifications to which you have access. These modifications alter the abilities or form of your light mortar. ",
          "kind": "text",
          "marks": {
            "bold": false,
            "italic": false,
            "superscript": false
          }
        }
      ],
      "kind": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "embed",
          "resolved": true,
          "target": "siege-weapon/light-mortar"
        }
      ],
      "kind": "paragraph"
    },
    {
